--- a/.andromeda/architecture.md
+++ b/.andromeda/architecture.md
@@ -84,3 +84,2 @@
 decision/every-send-confirmed · Every send is confirmed — A send not matched by a prompt-submitted within the confirmation window is reported not-delivered with detail no-prompt-submitted. · why: A turn boundary per the hooks does not prove the input box is ready; confirmation is the backstop behind the screen gate.
-decision/exact-prompt-match · Exact prompt match after agent normalisation — The typed text is matched exactly against prompt-submitted's text, whatever its origin, after the agent crate removes the long-paste wrapper and its frame and reverses tag escaping, so the wrapper-side matcher never sees a Claude-specific shape.
 decision/exclusive-endpoint-bind · Exclusive endpoint bind — A start binds its endpoint exclusively, and a bind that finds the name taken is an exit-1 refusal, squatted-name. · why: So two concurrent starts cannot both win.
@@ -181,2 +180,3 @@
 decision/self-describing-frames-no-handshake · Self-describing frames, no handshake — Every channel `params` carries `v` and the sender's `CARGO_PKG_VERSION`, with no handshake. · why: Mixed binary versions are a measured fact, so every frame self-describes.
+decision/send-flight-lock · Send post-gate section under the wrapper flight lock — A send's post-gate section, the human-typing and turn-running reads, the link record, send-issued and the paste, runs under one wrapper flight lock that the hook.event claim, turn start and end and wheel moves also take; a human key never takes the lock. · why: Closes the race between the readiness gate and a turn the wrapper learns of, while the human's keys never wait.
 decision/send-never-queued · A send mid-turn or mid-send is refused, never queued — A `send` while a turn runs or while another `send` is in flight is refused `not-delivered` with detail `turn-running`, never queued, and nothing is typed for it.
@@ -197,2 +197,3 @@
 decision/start-pins-the-bytes-it-checked · Start pins the very bytes it checked — A start reads its own exe once, keys the home-tree check by those bytes and pins those same bytes, so the copy it runs is the copy whose folders it checked. · why: The strict-modes check of the pinned copy's bin and plugin folders and the pinned-hash-mismatch refusal both assume no second read of the exe.
+decision/submitted-form-prompt-match · Prompt match in the submitted form after agent normalisation — The typed text matches prompt-submitted's text, whatever its origin, after the agent crate removes the long-paste wrapper and frame and reverses tag escaping, when equal or when non-empty and equal to the typed text less its trailing run of ASCII space, TAB, CR and LF. · why: The CLI trims whitespace at submit; the trim set is an assumption not yet read live, and trimming at either end is held as the candidate. · provisional
 decision/sync-core-tokio-only-in-mcp · Hybrid sync core, Tokio only in mcp — The core is synchronous, and Tokio is confined to the `mcp` subcommand; among the product crates only `viola-mcp` enables `tokio`. · why: portable-pty's handles are blocking, so the pump needs threads either way; `hook` must not pay for runtime startup; rmcp and interprocess-async require Tokio. · guard: sole-root `cargo deny` `tokio` ban (`deny-sync.toml`) and a `cargo check` of the sync crates on `ubuntu-latest` · except: `viola-channel`'s optional `tokio` feature, enabled by `viola-mcp`; its graph without the feature is proven tokio-free.
@@ -509,3 +510,3 @@
 contract/channel-methods/hook-dialog-unverified-cli · channel methods · hook.dialog unverified CLI — On an unverified CLI the wrapper replies `null` to `hook.dialog` at once.
-contract/channel-methods/hook-event-driver-origin · channel methods · hook.event driver origin — A `prompt-submitted` equal to the in-flight `send`'s typed text is appended with `origin:"driver"`, and only then settles that send.
+contract/channel-methods/hook-event-driver-origin · channel methods · hook.event driver origin — A `prompt-submitted` that is the in-flight `send`'s typed text, or a non-empty text equal to it less its trailing run of ASCII space, TAB, CR and LF, is appended with `origin:"driver"`, its text kept as submitted, and only then settles that send.
 contract/channel-methods/last · channel methods · last — A request: `last` `{from?}` answers `{last_assistant_message:<string|null>, ts:<string|null>}`: both `null` before any turn; a `turn-ended` whose message is not a string gives `null` plus its `ts`.
@@ -587,3 +588,3 @@
 contract/hook-event/appended-line · channel hook.event · appended line — A valid event is appended as {v, ts:<append time>, instance, kind, source:"hook", data}.
-contract/hook-event/driver-relabel · channel hook.event · driver relabel — A prompt-submitted whose text equals the in-flight send's typed text is appended with origin driver and only then settles that send.
+contract/hook-event/driver-relabel · channel hook.event · driver relabel — A prompt-submitted whose text is the in-flight send's typed text, or a non-empty text equal to it less its trailing run of ASCII space, TAB, CR and LF, is appended with origin driver, its text kept as submitted, and only then settles that send.
 contract/hook-event/kind · channel hook.event · kind — One of session-start, prompt-submitted, turn-ended, session-end, activity; data is an object; an invalid event is not appended and an append failure is -32603.
